flowchart TB
  Q[Substantive question & target population] --> E[Specify intervention, outcomes, timing]
  E --> PO[Potential outcomes & estimand: ATE, ATT, ITT, LATE, CATE]
  E --> SC[SCM / DAG: causes, colliders, mediators, selection]
  PO --> ID{What source of identifying variation?}
  SC --> ID
  ID --> R[Randomized assignment]
  ID --> O[Measured confounding, observational treatment]
  ID --> P[Policy or quasi-experimental variation]
  ID --> T[Sequential treatment over time]
  R --> RI[Randomization inference / covariate adjustment]
  O --> CA[Conditional exchangeability, positivity, consistency]
  CA --> EST[Regression / matching / IPW / AIPW]
  P --> DID[Parallel trends: DiD, event study]
  P --> SYN[Donor trends: synthetic control]
  P --> IV[Instrument: exclusion & relevance]
  P --> RD[Continuity at cutoff: RD]
  T --> LONG[Sequential exchangeability: g-methods, MSM]
  RI --> INF[Sampling & assignment-aware inference]
  EST --> INF
  DID --> INF
  SYN --> INF
  IV --> INF
  RD --> INF
  LONG --> INF
  INF --> VAL[Diagnostics: balance, overlap, pre-trends, placebo, weak IV, sorting]
  VAL --> SEN[Sensitivity, hidden bias, spillovers, missingness]
  SEN --> H[Heterogeneity, generalization, policy value]
  H --> REP[Replicable causal research report & decisions]
  SC --> GRAPH[Back-door, front-door & causal discovery]
  GRAPH --> CA
  H --> ML[Optional meta-learners, orthogonality, DML]
  ML --> REP
